      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>user</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>User is a SELinux user label that applies to the container.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
      <h3 id="_specinstallspecdeploymentsspectemplatespecephemeralcontainerssecuritycontextseccompprofile" class="group scroll-mt-20">.spec.install.spec.deployments[].spec.template.spec.ephemeralContainers[].securityContext.seccompProfile<a href="#_specinstallspecdeploymentsspectemplatespecephemeralcontainerssecuritycontextseccompprofile" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Description</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>The seccomp options to use by this container. If seccomp options are provided at both the pod &amp; container level, the container options override the pod options. Note that this field cannot be set when spec.os.name is windows.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Type</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><CodeBlock code={"`object`"} lang="plaintext" /></dd>
